WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.667
-Bowen Yang, I want to talk
about your new movie,

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.234
"Fire Island,"
but this is true.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:08.133
You just got back from --
from vacation.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.934
-From vacation in Fire Island.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:13.501
We went buck wild
and watched "The Hours,"

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:15.968
starring Nicole Kidman
and Meryl Streep

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:17.501
and Julianne Moore.
-Yeah, wait. Sorry.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.400
-You said you went buck wild.
-I went buck wild.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.968
-Fire Island is like party,
like -- [ Imitates air horn ]

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.100
Yeah, air horn.
-Air horn, but for us,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.801
it was "Mrs. Dalloway
will get the flowers herself."

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:31.467
It was, like, very --
like, so -- we were going crazy

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:35.067
by watching "The Hours."
-You didn't go to high tea?

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.300
-We went to high tea,
but the highlight was really,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.067
like,
people coming to our house,

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.167
thinking we were partying,
and then it was just

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.734
a dark living room with the glow
of Meryl Streep.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.300
-Meryl Streep.
The glow of Meryl Streep.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.868
-The glow of Meryl Streep.
-It's hard to beat that.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:50.033
Well, you have
a very interesting thing.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.267
I know it's the start of summer,

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.634
and I just want
to talk to you about this.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:56.100
You are -- You have an issue
in a popular summer trend.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.834
You are afraid of White Claw.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:02.000
-I'm afraid of White Claw.
-That's on your IMDb page.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.200
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, it is.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.667
-But why are you afraid
of that beverage?

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.634
-Here's the thing,
and go with me on this.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.567
Because seltzer itself
is already too much.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:15.067
It's like spicy bubbly water.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.734
And so to make it alcoholic

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.067
is just a hat on top of a hat,
right?

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.400
[ Laughter ]
And, like,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.901
the cans are too tall,

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:24.200
and they're staring me down
in the fridge.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.033
I still have White Claw
from last year in my fridge.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.868
Everyone, stop!
Everyone's not on my side

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.634
with this.
-No, we're on your side!

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:34.834
-Come on! Boo!
-All right, all right!

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:37.200
-No, no, no.
We love White Claw.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.267
-But have you tried it?
-I've tried it.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.400
But I -- you know what?
-It's too much.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.901
-It's too much.
But I just heard that

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.133
the official drink of the summer
is a Dirty Shirley.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.133
And I was drinking
Shirley Temples

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.634
way back in middle school
at Chili's or whatever.

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.100
-What is a --
-What is a Dirty Shirley?

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.267
It's a Shirley Temple with,
like, vodka in it or something.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.601
-Wow.
-And so that's --

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:58.133
Aperol Sprtiz is over,
and now Dirty Shirleys are in,

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.267
and so I feel like
I'm ahead of the trend.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.000
And...
-I mean...

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.334
-Speaking of
ahead of the trends...

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.133
-Oh!
-I saw you on the season finale.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.701
By the way, another great season
of Bowen Yang,

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.300
"Saturday Night Live," huh?
Not too shabby.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
Here you are, season finale

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.501
of "Saturday Night Live,"
the Trendsetters.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.567
-Yes.
-Gosh, it made me laugh so much.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.634
Is that Dirty --
-That might be a Dirty Shirley.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.634
-Might be a Dirty Shirley.
-Definitely not a hard seltzer.

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.567
-No, definitely not.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.067
This was Aidy's last show.
-It was.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.267
-It was Kate McKinnon's
last show,

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.400
it was Kyle Mooney's,
Pete Davidson.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.567
-Like, four people who defined
what the show was so long.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.334
-Was it emotional? I've been
there when people leave.

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:39.234
It's always --
For me, it's a little --

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.200
I feel like I just want to step
away and let them have their --

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.767
-Yeah.
I basically did that.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:45.467
But I was still a jerk,
and at good-nights,

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.267
