and they probably imagined

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.667
what this moment would be like,
their last good-nights.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.501
And I was just off to the side
but still, like,

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.667
sneaking a photo in.
I felt like such a --

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:57.033
such a paparazzi jerk.
Anyway, I mean, after that,

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.234
we just went to the after-party
and ate pigs in a blanket.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:02.167
-Yeah, that's how you do it!
That's how you party.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.300
-That's how you party, and Lorne
loves a pig in a blanket.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.267
-He does?
-He likes -- Wait.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.200
Didn't he --
I feel pigs in a blanket

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.334
is one of those Lorne lore
things that has been there

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:16.200
since, like,
the show has existed.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.767
-Pigs in a blanket?
-What are you talking --

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.934
You know -- You know this.
-I know Lorne,

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.167
but I don't know
pigs in a blanket.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.901
-Okay.
He loves pigs in a blanket.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.200
-Well, who doesn't love
pigs in a blanket?

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.701
-There you go.
-I mean, right?

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.267
-Yeah!
-Popcorn I know,

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.901
but I didn't know about
pigs in a blanket.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.567
-Pigs in a blanket.
That's, like, part of mythology.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:33.701
The mythos of Lorne.
-I want to talk to you, also,

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.968
